# Format the tree rather than `--staged`.
#
# Biome treats explicitly-passed paths as in-scope even when `files.includes`
# excludes them, so `--staged` fails the commit as soon as a staged file is
# outside the configured globs (a Markdown doc, a `.sql` migration, or the
# archived trees under trope-cards/versions/). Passing the root lets Biome
# apply its own include list, which is what defines what this project owns.
#
# The risk of this over `--staged` is that it can format unstaged working-tree
# files too. That is safe here because formatting is idempotent and the only
# thing that must not be reformatted is already excluded above.
bunx biome format --write .
